CAT = "maceEthics"; SEG = "ETH"
Q = [
('Which quality does the model curriculum name as central to the working relationship between nurses and assistive personnel?',
 'Trust', ['Authority', 'Efficiency', 'Independence'],
 'The model curriculum says trust is central to the working relationship, built on two-way communication, initiative, appreciation and willingness to help each other.'),
('A medication aide wants to know the usual side effects of a drug the facility rarely stocks. Which written reference fits best?',
 'Package insert', ['MAR', "Resident's care plan", 'Pharmacy invoice'],
 'The package or drug insert and drug reference manuals list uses, side effects and precautions. The nurse, pharmacist and physician are the people resources.'),
('A tablet looks different from the one the resident usually gets, though the label matches. Which professional is best placed to say whether the product changed?',
 'Pharmacist', ['Prescribing physician', 'Facility administrator', 'Senior medication aide'],
 'The pharmacist dispenses the medication and can confirm a change of manufacturer or a dispensing error. The aide holds the dose and tells the nurse as facility policy directs.'),
('A medication aide often jokes with a resident and has started sharing personal problems with her. What is the main risk?',
 'Boundary problem', ['Confidentiality breach', 'Delegation problem', 'Neglect report'],
 "The model curriculum covers setting boundaries. Sharing personal problems shifts the relationship toward the aide's needs rather than the resident's."),
("A medication aide pockets a resident's unused pain tablets to take home. What is this called?",
 'Drug diversion', ['Medication waste', 'A refused dose', 'Falsifying a record'],
 'Diversion is moving a medication away from its intended use. The model curriculum lists diversion, theft and fraud among the legal issues an aide must know.'),
('An aide charts that a dose was given, though it was never given. Which legal issue is this?',
 'Falsifying a record', ['Drug diversion', 'Client abandonment', 'Breach of privacy'],
 'Documenting care that was not done is fraud in the record. It can hide a missed dose and lead to harm.'),
('A resident has bruises on both upper arms in the shape of fingers, and he flinches when a certain visitor arrives. What should the aide recognize?',
 'Possible physical abuse', ['Possible neglect', 'Medication side effect', 'Possible financial abuse'],
 'The model curriculum names physical, verbal, psychological, sexual and financial abuse and the duty to report it. Patterned bruises and fear of a person are warning signs.'),
('A staff member tells a resident she will lose her phone privileges if she complains about her care. Which type of abuse is this?',
 'Psychological abuse', ['Financial abuse', 'Physical abuse', 'Neglect of care'],
 'Threats and intimidation that cause fear are psychological abuse, one of the types the model curriculum says must be reported.'),
('A staff member regularly mocks a resident and calls him names. Which type of abuse is this?',
 'Verbal abuse', ['Financial abuse', 'Physical abuse', 'Neglect'],
 'Mocking, insults and name-calling are verbal abuse. The aide reports it as facility policy and state law direct.'),
('An aide gives a resident the wrong medication and the resident is harmed. Which legal claim does this expose the aide to?',
 'Negligence claim', ['Fraud claim', 'Theft charge', 'Diversion charge'],
 'Failing to meet the accepted standard of care, causing harm, is the basis of a negligence or malpractice claim. Following the rights and checks each time is the defense.'),
('Under the model curriculum, which step is part of building relationships with clients?',
 'Removing listening barriers', ['Speaking for the client', 'Sharing personal stories', 'Keeping visits brief'],
 'The model curriculum reviews the communication process and barriers to effective listening and communication, along with setting boundaries and team building.'),
('A medication aide is unsure what a drug on the MAR is for. Which source should the aide check before giving it?',
 'Drug reference manual', ['MAR alone', "Resident's care plan", 'Coworker on another unit'],
 'The model curriculum lists the nurse, pharmacist, physician, package insert and drug reference manuals as resources for medication questions.'),
]
